  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="eaa30d5a-be1c-53cd-98a4-81bc4b36acf7" activityNameId="f82fdfc0-3772-5d8b-a317-9970735c5308" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Wood chips, from industry, softwood, burned in furnace 300kW - ohne Holzinput</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Wood chips, from industry, softwood, burned in furnace 300kW - ohne Holzinput
Heat of combustion of wood based on low heating value. The apparent density of the chips (humidity = 40%) is 237 kg/m3, the bulk density is 169 kg/m3, and the low heating value is 3162 MJ/m3. Air emission factors from measurements were adjusted based on operation experience of installed furnace. The inventory shall be considered valid also for boilers with nominal capacity in the approximate range of 100 to 700 kW. ;
UUID: 8e90122c-d629-31c4-83c1-aa6d953e5600
This module describes the combustion of natural wood chips. Included are the infrastructure, the wood requirements (softwood chips from industry, u=40%), the emissions to air, the transport of the fuel, the electricity needed for operation, and the disposal of the ashes.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Boiler of average technology available on market. 
Time period: Some emission data used to calculate averages are from the second half of the 1990´s.
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_8e90122c-d629-31c4-83c1-aa6d953e5600.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
